<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">International Court of Justice</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as World Court</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The International Court of Justice is the principal judicial organ of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a>, set up in 1945 and sitting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a>. It settles legal disputes between states and gives advisory opinions. Its 1971 opinion declared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a> illegal, and it has heard cases such as Nauru's claim over phosphate mining and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>–Belize dispute.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/international-court-of-justice.jpg" alt="International Court of Justice" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: public domain; vectorised by FOX 52 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:International_Court_of_Justice_Seal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
